  "_comment": "One entry per folder CI builds. 'upstream' names the folders whose change can break this one; the change detector runs a folder when it or anything upstream of it changes. 'dotnet' configures the .NET job (absent for a folder with no .NET build; 'release-pack' names the one project a release packs instead of the solution; 'state-machine' installs Trax.Api.StateMachine's npm packages first, for tests that run its generators under node; 'playwright' installs chromium, and the npm packages of Trax.Api.StateMachine and the Recovery page, which the browser tests build, Trax.Docs/adr/0049; 'api-dashboard' installs the npm packages of Trax.Api.Dashboard's React app before the build, which compiles it into the package); 'adr' configures the ADR guard over that folder's corpus. 'suites' are test projects carved out of a folder into a job of their own: one runs when anything in its 'upstream' (closed over like a folder's) or under one of its 'paths' changed, its folder's own job leaves it out with that row's 'test-args' filter, and its 'dotnet' takes the same keys as a folder's, with 'chromium' to install the browser.",
